From 4de313c86c324ad40c265c0f7299a6608411b3ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:49:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(v2): stop the agent writer from rewriting its own output
 on every boot

Three causes made the v2 host rewrite four agent files at every plugin init: the agent loader re-ingested files the host itself had written (one '(opencode) ' description prefix per boot), a display name and its hidden config-key alias that differ only by case shared one file on a case-insensitive filesystem, and the user agents dir was loaded a second time as project agents when the project directory is the home directory. Skip stamped files in the loader, give a case-colliding file a single owner, and never load the user agents dir twice.
---
